 | Specialized polynomial square | The schoolbook base case computes one diagonal plus one doubled cross product, while recursion uses three exact squares. Differential tests cover coefficient counts 1--195 around every threshold, nonmonic/repeated moduli, high-degree pre-reduction, adversarial coefficients, zero, alias, and constant cases. Reverse-order p125 pairs improved roots 1.08899x, SEA 1.07060x, and wall 1.06837x with identical 55-level projections and final trace. |
